jobs.description:
Position overview

The Technology Executive Director is responsible for converting corporate technology strategy, product technology planning and key technology projects into specific execution plans, and overseeing the implementation, delivery, resource allocation and cross-team collaboration of technology projects.

This position focuses on connecting technology strategy and actual implementation, ensuring that engineering, R&D, IT, product and architecture teams collaborate efficiently around unified goals and complete key technology projects as planned.

Core responsibilities

1. Technology Strategy Execution
Translate corporate and technical department strategies into annual execution plans;
Develop technology project roadmaps, priorities and key milestones;
Oversee implementation of technology strategic plans;
Identify technical and resource barriers to implementation;
Regularly report execution progress to CTO, CIO or technical senior management.

2. Technical project management
Responsible for the overall execution of major technical projects;
Establish project plans, timelines and delivery standards;
Track project progress, budget, resources and risks;
Promote timely correction of delayed or high-risk projects;
Ensure technical projects are delivered on time and with high quality.

3. Cross-departmental technical collaboration
Coordinate product, engineering, R&D, IT, data and security teams;
Clarify the responsibilities and delivery boundaries of different teams;
Drive cross-departmental technology projects;
Resolve execution conflicts between teams;
Establish a unified communication mechanism for technical projects.

4. Technical operation management
Optimize the daily execution process of the technical team;
Establish technical operational KPIs and performance indicators;
Promote the standardization of R&D and engineering processes;
Improve technology delivery efficiency;
Establish a technology execution management mechanism.

5. Engineering and R&D Delivery
Oversee software and technology product development programs;
Collaborate with Engineering, R&D and Product teams;
Manage development cycles and release plans;
Promote Agile, Scrum, DevOps and other practices;
Improve project delivery quality and efficiency.

6. Technical Infrastructure Execution
Oversee infrastructure upgrades and technology platform construction;
Coordinate technical teams such as Cloud, Infrastructure, and Network;
Promote system modernization and architecture upgrade projects;
Manage technology migration and systems integration projects;
Ensure stable delivery of infrastructure projects.

7. Technology risk management
Identify technology project and system execution risks;
Establish project risk registration and response mechanisms;
Supervise the resolution of major technical issues;
Collaborate with CTO, CIO, CISO and related teams;
Ensure business continuity for critical technology projects.

8. Technical resources and budget
Participate in technical annual budget planning;
Manage project personnel and technical resource allocation;
Optimize resources based on project priorities;
Oversee technical project costs;
Improve the utilization rate of technical resources.

9. Team Management
Manage teams such as Technical Program Managers and Technology Operations Managers;
Mentor technical project leaders;
Establish a team performance management system;
Cultivate technical execution and project management talents;
Build a high-performing technology delivery culture.

Qualifications

Educational background
Bachelor degree or above in computer science, information technology, software engineering, engineering management or related majors;
MBA, technical management or project management related master's degree is preferred;
Certifications such as PMP, PgMP, and Agile are preferred.

work experience
20+ years of technology, engineering, IT or project management experience;
More than 15 years of technical project or technical operation management experience;
Priority will be given to those with experience in Director of Technology, Director of Technical Program Management, Director of Engineering Operations and other positions;
Have experience in large-scale technical project and cross-department project management;
Priority will be given to those with experience in enterprise-level technology transformation or system construction.

core competencies
Technology Execution
Technical Program Management
Technology Operations
Engineering Delivery
Project Portfolio Management
Agile/Scrum
DevOps
Technology Strategy Execution
Resource Planning
Risk Management
Cross-functional Leadership
Performance Management

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
Technical project completion rate on schedule;
Project budget achievement rate;
technology delivery cycle;
Project milestone completion rate;
Technical project quality;
Major problem resolution cycle;
Engineering team productivity;
Technical resource utilization;
Technical project risk control rate;
Strategic technology project execution rate.

Show more

Show less

Seniority level

Director

Employment type

Part-time

Job function

Information Technology

